+# MASTER7 v155 game catalogue integrity release
+
+Release: `17.0.0-selfbuilt.155-catalogue-integrity`
+
+This release completes the next read-only catalogue integrity pass for the
+configured game suppliers.
+
+- Every non-direct supplier response must identify the exact requested
+  supplier. Malformed, duplicate, oversized or explicitly incomplete refreshes
+  preserve the last trusted snapshot under maintenance instead of publishing a
+  partial list.
+- JILI 1:1 and 1:100 use independent account caches and profile readiness.
+  Unknown per-title availability remains maintenance, and the sponsored JILI
+  entry opens the exact selected profile instead of an invalid brand ID.
+- 918KISS artwork uses the verified image URL stored for the exact profile and
+  game, rather than guessing a path from the game code.
+- Rectangle and GodeeZone direct catalogues reject unsafe IDs, names,
+  categories, duplicates and incomplete sets.
+- JDB and RSGHub explicitly attest catalogue completeness. RSGHub verifies the
+  response timestamp, rejects unsafe names and withholds unapproved remote
+  artwork.
+
+The public lobby remains truthful: 37 brands and 42 profiles may be listed,
+but no profile is Play-enabled until its supplier contract, launch, wallet,
+settlement and production acceptance evidence all pass.
+
+No player, launch, balance, wallet, transfer, settlement, recovery or payment
+operation is enabled by this release. VPay, GSPAY, 1MPay, payment switches,
+credentials, service plans, DNS and database schema are unchanged.
